# Flow-manager browser-turn monitoring

This rule carries only shared Browser-GPT transport guidance. Workflow-specific
authoring, review, disposition, acceptance, PR readiness, and merge authority
remain with their owning skills/runbooks.

## Launch and observation

Use the shared one-turn runbook:
[Preflight](../../docs/browser-gpt-turn-runbook.md#start-of-shift-preflight),
[Prepare](../../docs/browser-gpt-turn-runbook.md#prepare-one-turn),
[Launch](../../docs/browser-gpt-turn-runbook.md#launch), and
[Observe](../../docs/browser-gpt-turn-runbook.md#observe-and-settle).

One invocation has one stable input and one send-capable transport owner.
Possible/proven delivery never authorizes a blind resend. Timeout, child exit,
missing local output, or missing terminal envelope is not proof of non-delivery.
Recover only the same owned invocation/conversation.

## Diagnostic probe

The page probe is read-only diagnostic evidence. It may classify the exact owned
conversation when ordinary observation is insufficient, but never sends,
retries, mutates workflow state, or grants acceptance authority.

## Pack-review retry observation

Pack-review retains its own runner/review authority. Browser-GPT transport may
observe or recover an exact reviewer conversation, but it does not create an
extra review round, bypass a review cap, or rewrite current-head review state.
